<title>FRANCE: Cr Lyonnais hopes for breakeven.</title>
<headline>Cr Lyonnais hopes for breakeven.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-11-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Credit Lyonnais chairman Jean Peyrelevade said in an interview on Saturday that he hoped the troubled French bank would break even in 1996 after reporting a first-half profit of 67 million francs ($13.1 million).</p>
<p>&quot;For the full year, it's not a forecast, it's a hope. I hope we will remain in the same situation -- that we will be able to tend toward breakeven after having fully provisioned for restructuring to the end of 1998,&quot; he told Radio Classique.</p>
</text>
